// REJECTED — an EXTERN config field whose declared type is a transparent alias.
// Same rule as the component case (item 378, config is static data), and a
// different diagnostic, because the erasure the reference performs is not the
// same on both owners: it substitutes a component's config field types and does
// NOT substitute an extern's. The alias declaration is dropped either way, so by
// the time the extern's config block is judged, `Handler` names nothing at all.
//
// A head that resolves to no declaration proves nothing about the field being
// data, so it is refused as opaque rather than waved through (item 378). That is
// the honest answer: naming the arrow behind the alias would be reporting a
// resolution the reference never performed here.
//
// expected error:
//   config field `on_row` of extern `load_rows` has type `Handler`, which
//   reaches the opaque type `Handler`; a config field must be static data

type Handler = (Int) -> Str

extern pure fn load_rows(path: Str) -> Str
  config { on_row: Handler }
  = @py { return path }
